  "narrative": "The new wave largely resolves the feature_003 question as a negative finding. The marginal feature_003 association is below the 0.15 composite dependency-score threshold (+0.139 [0.065, 0.213]). In the largest clean feature_010=0/feature_037=0 stratum, feature_003 remains below threshold (+0.135 [0.064, 0.206]), and in feature_037=1 and feature_010=0/feature_037=1 strata it is near zero (+0.082 [-0.063, 0.228] and +0.071 [-0.063, 0.205]). The only conditional estimates with point estimates above threshold occur in feature_010=1-related strata (+0.188 [0.045, 0.332] and +0.178 [0.040, 0.316]), but those cells are smaller, the intervals are wide and include effects well below threshold, and the pattern is not consistent across feature_037 strata. Given the multiplicity of feature_003 tests and the lack of a coherent estimate above threshold with supportive uncertainty, I reject the feature_003 track rather than keep it active. The core marker robustness analyses are decisive: after conditioning on the other core marker and feature_003=0, feature_037 remains strongly associated with stronger dependency (H54 +0.845 [0.787, 0.903]; H55 +0.764 [0.644, 0.884]), and feature_010=0 versus 1 also remains strongly associated (H56 +0.835 [0.772, 0.899]; H57 +0.917 [0.800, 1.034]). H60 and H61 show that both core associations also have large subgroup contrasts in feature_021=0, although these are subgroup robustness checks rather than formal interactions. Broad screens H62 and H63 provide no support in the claimed direction. I do not request validation because the two central marginal associations H16 and H39 are already independently validated and the new accepted conditional effects are robustness demonstrations rather than new central claims requiring independent confirmation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 appraise update: Close feature_003 as a supported predictor. Marginal and clean conditional estimates are below the 0.15 threshold; only small feature_010=1 strata have inconsistent over-threshold point estimates with lower bounds far below threshold. Rejected/closed: H18, H42, H46, H47, H52, H53, H58, H59. Accepted robustness claims: H54-H57 show feature_037 and feature_010 associations persist conditional on the other core marker and feature_003=0; H60-H61 show large feature_037 and feature_010 contrasts in the feature_021=0 subgroup, but not formal interactions. H62 feature_033 and H63 feature_016 are null/opposite near-zero and closed. Stable accepted core findings remain H16 and H39, both independently validated, with complementary conditional support from earlier H40/H41/H43/H44 and now H54-H57. No validation requested. Next iteration can return to broad exploration among remaining active untested screens, but the two validated core predictors should remain the scientific center unless a new estimate has a lower bound clearly above 0.15."
