  "narrative": "This wave produces one important new signal and several important negative/robustness results. H20 tested feature_002=1 versus 0 with the pre-specified negative-direction hypothesis. R51 has a very large interval, but it is on the opposite side of the signed scale: estimate -0.810 with 95% CI [-0.875, -0.745]. Because the signed estimate is negative when the claim direction is -1, this rejects the registered H20 hypothesis. However, the underlying raw contrast is very large in magnitude: feature_002=1 versus 0 appears associated with a higher composite dependency score by about 0.81 units, equivalently feature_002=0 versus 1 is associated with stronger dependency by about 0.81 units. That is far above the 0.15-unit scientific threshold and warrants a new reversed claim. I registered a reversed feature_002 main-effect claim linked to H20 and proposed conditional feature_002 tests within core-marker strata to determine whether this is an independent association, a proxy for feature_010/feature_037, or a stratified/confounded pattern.\n\nH21 and H36 are clear null screens. feature_048=1 versus 0 has signed estimate -0.005 [-0.079, 0.068], and feature_021=0 versus 1 has signed estimate -0.031 [-0.107, 0.045]. Neither supports the registered direction, and both are too small to be scientifically meaningful. These claims are closed.\n\nThe feature_003 conditional core-marker analyses strongly support the established core associations rather than feature_003 as an explanatory variable. Within feature_003=1, feature_037=1 versus 0 has signed estimate +0.752 [0.604, 0.900], and feature_010=0 versus 1 has +0.779 [0.632, 0.925]. Both lower bounds are far above the threshold, so H64 and H65 are accepted as conditional robustness demonstrations. The corresponding feature_003 interaction tests, H66 and H67, are near zero and imprecise around zero: feature_037 interaction with feature_003=1 is -0.065 [-0.227, 0.098], and feature_010 interaction with feature_003=1 is -0.063 [-0.224, 0.098]. These do not support effect modification by feature_003 and are rejected/closed.\n\nThe feature_021 interaction tests also do not support effect modification. H72, the feature_021=0 interaction for feature_037, is -0.079 [-0.254, 0.096]; H73, the feature_021=0 interaction for feature_010, is +0.043 [-0.124, 0.210]. Both intervals include zero and the point estimates are below the 0.15-unit threshold. Combined with the null feature_021 main effect in H36, feature_021 is not a useful effect modifier in the supplied dataset, though the earlier accepted feature_021=0 subgroup contrasts remain robustness checks.\n\nH4-H6 are invalid because the +1 versus -1 contrasts for continuous standardized signatures produced zero cells in the required comparison cells. These are not substantive null results; the exact specification is untestable. I closed them as exact comparison specifications and did not request validation. The signatures have already been probed through several interactions with the core markers, with no evidence of effect modification, so further effort is better focused on the newly discovered feature_002 track.\n\nI did not request validation this iteration. The strongest central effects feature_037 and feature_010 are already independently validated. The new feature_002 signal is promising but currently appears on the opposite side of the original registered claim, and its independence from the core markers still needs conditional tests. The reversed feature_002 claim and the proposed conditional feature_002 analyses are the highest-value next analyses; if the reversed feature_002 main association remains large after conditioning or if it becomes an accepted new central claim, it will be a strong validation candidate.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 appraise update: New main discovery: feature_002 main effect is very large but opposite to H20. R51 signed estimate for feature_002=1 vs 0 direction -1 is -0.810 [-0.875,-0.745], implying raw feature_002=1 vs0 positive, or feature_002=0 vs1 negative by about 0.810. Registered reversed feature_002=0 vs1 direction -1 with initial accept parent H20. Need conditional tests: feature_002=0 vs1 within feature_010=0/feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_010=1, feature_037=0; core markers within feature_002=0. Purpose: test independence vs proxy/confounding for feature_010/feature_037. Central validated markers: H16 feature_037=1 vs0; H39 feature_010=0 vs1. Conditional core robustness now includes feature_003=1: H64 feature_037 +0.752 [0.604,0.900]; H65 feature_010 +0.779 [0.632,0.925]. feature_003 interactions H66/H67 null and closed. feature_021 main H36 null, interactions H72/H73 null and closed. feature_048 main H21 null and closed. H4-H6 exact continuous signature contrasts +1 vs -1 invalid zero cells; closed as exact specs. Signatures not effect modifiers in prior tests. Next analyze should prioritize reversed feature_002/conditional feature_002 and core-in-feature_002=0 tests, then decide whether feature_002 is a new central accepted association and validate it. Avoid requesting validation until feature_002 reversed claim has direct ledger evidence or is accepted as a distinct claim. All conclusions are dataset associations, not causal/generalizable.",
