  "narrative": "The H39 response deadline concerns the feature_010=0 versus feature_010=1 marginal contrast in the signed stronger-dependency direction. The independent validation estimate is +0.788 composite dependency-score units with a strict independent interval [0.698, 0.878], while the discovery estimate was +0.829 [0.767, 0.891]. The validation lower bound is far above the 0.15-unit effect-size threshold and agrees closely with discovery, so I explicitly reassess H39 as accepted and closed. Together with H16, the supplied dataset now has two independently validated strong associations: feature_037=1 versus 0 and feature_010=0 versus 1 are each associated with stronger composite dependency by roughly 0.8 units. These are dataset-specific association claims, not causal or generalizable claims. The most important new discovery is feature_002. The original feature_002=1 versus 0 negative-direction claim was rejected because the large effect lay on the opposite side of the signed scale; the reversed claim H86, feature_002=0 versus 1 in the stronger-dependency direction, is supported by discovery with signed estimate +0.810 [0.745, 0.875]. H86 is therefore accepted as a new central dataset association, but it has not yet been independently validated and its relationship to feature_037/feature_010 must be resolved. If feature_002=0 remains associated with stronger dependency within strata of feature_010 and feature_037, it will be an additional independent candidate; if it attenuates, the marginal association may largely reflect correlation or confounding with the already validated core markers rather than a separate predictor signal. The next analyses are therefore stratified tests of feature_002 within feature_037=1 and within feature_010/feature_037 combinations, plus tests of feature_037 and feature_010 when feature_002=0, to disentangle independence from proxy effects. Supported negative findings include the feature_003 track, which is below threshold marginally and inconsistent conditionally; feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_024, feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_001, feature_048, feature_021, feature_033, and feature_016, which do not show meaningful effects in the tested directions; and most tested interactions among markers and research signatures, including feature_003 and feature_021 interactions with the core markers, which are near zero. The feature_037-by-feature_010 interaction H45 is also not supported as a meaningful positive interaction, though its interval does not exclude a modest difference. The exact +1 versus -1 continuous signature comparisons H4-H6 were invalid specifications rather than substantive nulls. Unresolved work includes validation of feature_002 and conditional independence tests, plus lower-priority untested broad screens such as feature_060, feature_035, feature_063, feature_046, feature_059, feature_014, feature_006, feature_017, feature_043, and feature_064.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 synthesis update. Accepted central dataset associations: H16 feature_037=1 vs0 (validated +0.823 [0.732,0.913]); H39 feature_010=0 vs1 (reassessed with validation +0.788 [0.698,0.878], accepted/closed). H39 response deadline handled. Conditional robustness accepted: feature_037 remains large in feature_010=0/1 and feature_003=1 strata; feature_010 remains large in feature_037=0/1 and feature_003=1 strata. H45 feature_037 by feature_010 interaction not accepted (point below threshold, interval includes zero and upper >0.15, so modest uncertainty remains). feature_003 closed unsupported; feature_021 main and interactions closed unsupported/null; feature_048 null. New major candidate H86 feature_002=0 vs1 accepted from reversed H20/R51: +0.810 [0.745,0.875], discovery only. Priority now: determine whether feature_002 is independent of feature_037/feature_010. Existing proposals H87-H92 test feature_002 conditional on core markers and core markers conditional on feature_002=0. New proposals add feature_002 within feature_037=1 and within joint feature_010/feature_037 cells, plus feature_037 within feature_010=0/feature_002=0 and feature_010 within feature_037=0/feature_002=0. Next appraise: if feature_002 conditional lower bounds remain >0.15 and core marker estimates remain >0.15 within feature_002=0, request validation of H86 and treat feature_002 as independent candidate. If feature_002 attenuates in joint strata, keep marginal H86 accepted but interpret as correlated/proxy/confounded rather than separate central predictor. Do not interpret any findings as causal, mechanistic, or generalizable."
