  "narrative": "All twelve newly returned comparisons have valid Welch cells and at least 20 observations in every cell, so the results can be interpreted as discovery evidence rather than specification failures. The central mixed-stratum contrasts are all very strong and far above the 0.15-unit effect-size threshold. H94 (feature_002=0 versus 1 within feature_010=0 and feature_037=1) is +0.722 [0.628,0.816]. H95 (feature_002 within feature_010=1 and feature_037=0) is +0.850 [0.765,0.936]. H96 (feature_037 within feature_010=0 and feature_002=0) is +0.814 [0.768,0.860]. H97 (feature_010 within feature_037=0 and feature_002=0) is +0.804 [0.757,0.850]. H106 (feature_037 within feature_002=0 and feature_010=1) is +0.778 [0.697,0.860]. H107 (feature_010 within feature_002=0 and feature_037=1) is +0.839 [0.758,0.920]. Because these are mean differences rather than interactions, they show that each of the three central marker contrasts remains large after conditioning on two other measured predictors in these mixed strata. They do not prove causal independence or rule out shared latent structure, but they argue against a simple proxy explanation within the measured set. Accept all six and close the specific stratum investigations.\n\nThe feature_040 quartile checks also support persistence of the central associations. H113 (feature_037 in low feature_040) is +0.799 [0.669,0.929]. H114 (feature_010 in low feature_040) is +0.864 [0.750,0.977]. H115 (feature_002 in low feature_040) is +0.673 [0.530,0.816]. H117 (feature_037 in high feature_040) is +0.753 [0.630,0.877]. All signed lower bounds are far above 0.15. H115 is somewhat attenuated relative with its marginal estimate near +0.81, but the lower bound remains extremely large, so the dataset-specific association is still scientifically meaningful. I accept and close H113, H114, H115, and H117.\n\nH116 tests formal low-feature_040 effect modification for feature_037. The signed interaction is near zero, -0.006 [-0.154,0.142]. The interval includes null and its upper bound is below the 0.15-unit threshold. This does not support meaningful effect modification in the claimed direction; I reject and close H116. It should not be interpreted as proof of homogeneity, only as no evidence for a threshold-sized modification in this sample.\n\nH23 is a broad screen of feature_035=1 versus 0. The signed estimate is +0.020 [-0.061,0.101], which is null in the registered direction and below the effect-size threshold. Reject and close H23.\n\nCritical audit: the new mixed-stratum tests are multiply performed, but the accepted lower bounds are mostly 0.6 to 0.9 units, orders of magnitude above the 0.15-unit threshold, so they would remain scientifically meaningful under stringent multiplicity correction. The main interpretive limits are causal and mechanistic: these predictors are opaque, and conditioning on measured binary predictors cannot exclude mediation, collider-induced associations, correlated latent variables, or dataset-specific measurement artifacts. Independent validation is not requested here because the three central marginal associations (feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002) already have independent validation, while these new results are conditional or stratum-specific robustness checks rather than newly discovered independent signals. Validation resources are better reserved for any future large unvalidated predictor signal or for an ambiguous central claim.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise update. Newly accepted robust conditional/stratum results: H94-H97 and H106-H107 show the three central markers retain lower bounds above ~0.6 in mixed feature_002/feature_010/feature_037 strata. H113-H115 and H117 show persistence in feature_040 quartiles, with H115 modestly attenuated for feature_002 but still lower bound 0.530. H116 and H23 are null/negative and closed. The evidence now supports three dataset-specific strong association tracks: feature_037=1 versus 0, feature_010=0 versus 1, and feature_002=0 versus 1, all validated marginally and reinforced by conditional/subgroup analyses. These remain association claims only, not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims. No validation requested this wave because no new independent predictor was discovered and the central marginals are already independently validated. Next priorities: run H108/H109 if cells are feasible to complete central feature_002=1 mixed strata; run formal interactions H110-H112 to test homogeneity around core-marker/feature_002 relationships; continue broad screens including H118/H119 and the active binary screens; keep H98 deferred/closed if sparse because the all-positive triple may violate cell-count constraints. If H108/H109 or H110-H112 produce near-zero interactions and lower bounds above threshold, the interpretation becomes a very robust measured-marker pattern in this dataset. If attenuation or context dependence appears, revise toward correlated latent or contextual dependence while still avoiding causal language."
}

