  "narrative": "With validation budget exhausted, this exploration targets the main remaining unresolved scientific question: whether feature_063 and feature_003 represent independent residual signals, shared/redundant low-magnitude signals, or merely context-specific residual associations after conditioning on the four large major-track associations. The four large supplied-dataset associations remain feature_037=1 versus 0, feature_010=0 versus 1, feature_002=0 versus 1, and feature_027=1 versus 0. For direction -1 main effects, a positive signed estimate means the exposed level is associated with a more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. Threshold support requires a signed lower 95 percent bound above +0.15 composite dependency-score units. The first proposals test the joint structure of feature_063 and feature_003 within the all-major-reference core. P1 is an interaction of feature_063 with feature_003=0 versus feature_003=1; under direction -1, positive signed evidence means the feature_063 contrast is more negative when feature_003 is absent than when feature_003 is present, i.e. feature_003 attenuates or replaces the feature_063 residual. P2 is the reciprocal interaction of feature_003 with feature_063=0 versus feature_063=1; positive signed evidence means the feature_003 contrast is more negative when feature_063 is absent than when feature_063 is present, supporting shared residual structure. P3 through P7 are mean contrasts testing feature_063 and feature_003 in complementary major-reference backgrounds, with and without feature_027 restriction, to distinguish robust residual signal from selection artifacts, redundancy, or confounding by major tracks. The last four proposals are broad nominal categorical checks for untested levels of feature_052, feature_061, feature_062, and feature_059. Their direction is nominally chosen as -1 without an expectation. Low-prevalence conditional cells are possible; insufficient-cell diagnostics