  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no validation response deadline is pending; the voluntary independent-validation budget is exhausted. The synthesis therefore uses the complete supplied-dataset ledger plus previously delivered validation. All delivered estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so a positive signed value means the exposed level is associated with a more negative outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger composite dependency. The prespecified support rule for outcome_001 remains: a claimed negative-direction association is scientifically meaningful only when the signed lower 95% bound exceeds +0.15 composite dependency-score units. Insufficient-cell analyses are non-evidence, null interactions are not proof of independence, and all claims remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable effects.\n\nSupported findings. Four large binary associations are robustly supported and independently validated: feature_037=1 versus 0 (H16: discovery about +0.804, lower bound about +0.742; validation about +0.823, lower bound about +0.732), feature_010=0 versus 1 (H39: discovery about +0.829, lower bound about +0.767; validation about +0.788, lower bound about +0.698), feature_002=0 versus 1 (H86: discovery about +0.810, lower bound about +0.745; validation about +0.822, lower bound about +0.730), and feature_027=1 versus 0 (H139: discovery about +0.775, lower bound about +0.664; validation about +0.863, lower bound about +0.697). These are the principal durable supplied-dataset findings. They remain opaque-label associations and cannot be interpreted as mechanistic, causal, clinical-role, or generalizable claims.\n\nA narrower but scientifically useful finding is that feature_063=1 versus 0 is threshold-positive in specified major-reference backgrounds. The clean-core contrast H311 (feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_027=0, feature_003=0) has signed estimate about +0.285 and lower bound about +0.197. H254, using the four major-reference conditions but not restricting feature_003, has signed estimate about +0.260 and lower bound about +0.182. This supports a dataset-specific conditional feature_063 residual association, but it is not an accepted overall main effect, has not been independently validated, and is heavily shaped by predictor-selected conditioning and multiplicity. H311 also reuses R213, so it should not be treated as independent replication.\n\nNegative findings are broad. The constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 are null as main effects and as modifiers (H1-H3, H8-H10). feature_024 level_002 versus level_001 is null, and its feature_007 interaction is not supported after validation (H7, H11). Most low-prevalence binary predictors are below threshold or null, including feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_048, feature_060, feature_035, feature_033, feature_016, feature_013, feature_022, feature_028, feature_050, feature_064, feature_043, and feature_001. Numeric feature_053 contrasts and the examined feature_046 contrasts are not supported. feature_003 is not a robust independent residual track: overall H18 is below threshold, H42 and H306 validation lower bounds are far below +0.15, and the borderline conditional claims H295/H304 do not meet the lower-bound rule. Interaction evidence is also generally weak or null; for example, the feature_002 by feature_040 signal does not survive validation (H186/H211), and the feature_027 by feature_002 interaction is null after validation (H156).\n\nUnresolved uncertainty centers on feature_063 and its relationship to feature_003. The overall feature_063 main contrast H24 has a positive point estimate but a lower bound of about +0.145, just below the threshold, so I keep it unresolved and have deferred it rather than accept it. The reciprocal feature_063-feature_003 interaction tests H300 and H301 are algebraically identical and underpowered; their estimate about +0.111 with lower bound about -0.088 does not establish threshold-level joint structure. Conditional feature_063 contrasts when feature_003=1, including H266 and H303, are suggestive of attenuation but not threshold-supported. feature_003 borderline claims H295/H304 remain unresolved rather than accepted.\n\nThe most informative next analysis I registered is a less-selected but still controlled test of feature_063 among feature_003-positive participants conditioned on the two strongest opposite-direction major tracks, feature_010=0 and feature_037=0. This is more feasible than the tiny all-major-reference feature_003=1 joint cores and directly probes whether feature_063 retains a residual association when feature_003 is present. If the signed lower bound exceeds +0.15, this would strengthen the dataset-specific residual feature_063 interpretation; if it is null or below threshold, feature_063 is more plausibly attenuated in feature_003-positive contexts, correlated with feature_003, or limited to selected reference backgrounds. Without external data or remaining validation budget, this is the best remaining discovery-oriented follow-up.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 22 synthesize. No new validation delivered; validation budget exhausted. Decision rule: signed lower bound > +0.15 on outcome_001 for negative-direction claims. Four major validated binary tracks remain: feature_037=1 vs 0, feature_010=0 vs 1, feature_002=0 vs 1, feature_027=1 vs 0. Feature_063 is now supported as a narrow conditional residual in major-reference backgrounds: H311 clean core lower about +0.197 and H254 all-major-reference lower about +0.182, but H24 overall lower about +0.145 remains unresolved and is deferred. H311 reuses R213, so it is not independent replication. Feature_003 remains nonrobust; H295/H304 are borderline unresolved/deferred and should not be promoted. H300/H301 reciprocal feature_063-feature_003 interactions are identical and underpowered, not evidence of redundancy or independence. Most interactions and low-prevalence categorical checks are negative. Next analysis registered: feature_063=1 vs 0 in eligibility feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_003=1, a higher-powered redundancy/attenuation test; threshold-positive would strengthen feature_063 residual independent of feature_003, null would confine it to feature_003=0 or selected contexts. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations only."
