  "narrative": "All new estimates are signed to the registered negative direction, so positive values mean feature_063=1 is associated with a more negative composite dependency score. I applied the pre-specified threshold rule: accept only if the signed 95% Welch lower bound exceeds 0.15 with every cell at least 20. H331, H332, H333, and H334 meet this rule. H331 (feature_063=1 vs 0 when feature_038 is at least +0.5, unrestricted) is +0.519 with lower bound +0.349; H332 (full-population feature_063 interaction with feature_038 at least +0.5) is +0.408 with lower bound +0.208; H333 (clean-reference interaction with feature_038 at least +0.0) is +0.511 with lower bound +0.357; H334 (clean-reference mean with feature_038 at least +0.0) is +0.523 with lower bound +0.391. These support threshold-level dataset-specific feature_038-context associations for feature_063, especially a positive interaction with high feature_038. H330 is suggestive (+0.308) but its lower bound (+0.119) does not exceed 0.15, so it remains unresolved rather than accepted. H335 is a small or uncertain feature_036 context (+0.090; lower bound -0.084) and is rejected. H336 is signed in the opposite direction (-0.218; upper bound -0.012), so it does not support the claimed negative direction and is rejected. I closed H324 because its key conditional residual is now supported by formal feature_038-context evidence, and I closed H24 because the overall feature_063 contrast remains borderline while the more defensible claim is context dependence. The independent validation budget is exhausted, so no validation can be requested; these conclusions remain internal supplied-dataset associations among opaque predictors, with substantial multiplicity and selection risk from many context scans. They do not establish causality, biological mechanism, clinical meaning, confounding-adjusted effects, or generalizability.",
