  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no validation response deadline is pending; independent validation remaining is zero. I therefore make no validation-driven status changes. I close the remaining deferred unresolved feature_063 context investigations (H291, H295, H304, H315, H326) because no validation or further cell-adequate extension is available, but their evidence still does not satisfy the threshold rule, so their status remains unresolved.\n\nSupport rule: all outcome_001 claims were registered in the negative hypothesis direction, so positive signed estimates indicate that the exposed condition is associated with a more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. I accepted an association only when the signed lower 95% bound exceeded +0.15 composite dependency-score units and every cell had at least 20 observations. Insufficient-cell tests are non-evidence; null or imprecise interactions are not proof of absence. All interpretations are limited to associations in this supplied dataset among opaque predictor labels. They do not establish causality, biological mechanism, clinical meaning, confounding-adjusted effects, or external generalizability.\n\nSupported robust main tracks. Four binary contrasts are large, precise, and independently validated. feature_037=1 versus 0 (H16) has discovery +0.804, lower +0.742, and validation +0.823, lower +0.732. feature_010=0 versus 1 (H39) has discovery +0.829, lower +0.767, and validation +0.788, lower +0.698. feature_002=0 versus 1 (H86) has discovery +0.810, lower +0.745, and validation +0.822, lower +0.730. feature_027=1 versus 0 (H139) has discovery +0.775, lower +0.664, and validation +0.863, lower +0.697. These are the durable main findings: each exposed condition is associated with markedly stronger dependency than its comparator. The many accepted eligibility and subgroup replications of these tracks strengthen internal consistency but do not add independent external evidence.\n\nSupported conditional feature_063 finding. The overall feature_063=1 versus 0 contrast is positive but not threshold-supported as a main effect (H24, R214 +0.239, lower +0.145). However, feature_063 shows threshold-level residual associations in several restricted backgrounds, particularly after excluding or conditioning on the strongest opposite-direction tracks. The clean-reference result H243/H285/H299/H311 (R213) is +0.285, lower +0.197. The most informative new evidence supports feature_038 as a context for feature_063: H331 (unrestricted feature_038>=+0.5) is +0.519, lower +0.349; H332 (full-population interaction of feature_063 by feature_038>=+0.5) is +0.408, lower +0.208; H334 (clean reference mean with feature_038>=0.0) is +0.523, lower +0.391; and H333 (clean-reference interaction with feature_038>=0.0) is +0.511, lower +0.357. Together these support a dataset-specific feature_038-dependent feature_063 association, with stronger feature_063=1 association in higher feature_038 contexts. This is not an unconditional main effect, not causal, and not a mechanistic statement about a constructed standardized assay.\n\nPartial uncertainty in the feature_038 context. H330, the formal clean-reference interaction using feature_038>=+0.5, is suggestive (+0.308) but its lower bound is +0.119, below threshold; it remains unresolved. This does not disprove the accepted H324/H331/H332/H333/H334 evidence, but it shows that threshold-positive formal interaction depends on the chosen feature_038 cut point and cell sizes. The feature_036 probe did not support a comparable context effect: H335 is small and uncertain (+0.090, lower -0.084), and H336 is signed in the opposite claimed direction (-0.218, upper -0.012). Therefore feature_036 cannot be treated as a robust signature-axis modifier for feature_063.\n\nNegative and null findings. The constructed binary research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 are null as main effects and unsupported as interaction modifiers (H1-H3, H8-H10). feature_024 level_002 versus level_001 is unsupported as a main effect and its feature_007 interaction was not supported after validation (H7, H11). Most low-prevalence binary predictors failed the threshold rule or were precise/uncertain nulls, including feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_048, feature_060, feature_035, feature_033, feature_016, feature_013, feature_022, feature_028, feature_050, feature_064, feature_043, and feature_001. feature_003 is not a robust residual track: it is below threshold overall and in several clean or validated contexts, including H18, H42 validation, H191, and H306. Several categorical breadth probes and examined feature_053 numeric contrasts are not supported. Insufficient-cell feature_030, feature_062, and small feature_063 contexts are non-evidence, not negative findings.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. The principal remaining uncertainty is the extent to which the feature_063 finding reflects genuine context dependence versus selection among many conditional scans and limited validation power. Several borderline conditional or interaction contrasts remain unresolved, including H291, H295, H304, H315, H326, H330, and some earlier feature_063 interactions. H321 is invalid because one cell has fewer than 20 observations. Because the validation budget is exhausted, these cannot be upgraded without external data. The accepted feature_063 conditional results should be described as high-confidence internal conditional associations within the scanned contexts, not as established general predictors.\n\nMost informative next analysis. The highest-value next step would be a pre-specified external or true held-out validation of the exact feature_063 by feature_038 interaction on the same composite dependency-score scale, with cell-size adequacy and a single primary interaction estimate. Ideally this should be accompanied by a multiplicity-aware analysis or pre-registered model that includes the four robust main tracks, the feature_063 main contrast, and the feature_038 interaction, and that reports family-wise or false-discovery rate calibration. Additional within-dataset subgroup scans would have diminishing value. Only if the predictor labels acquire substantive biological or clinical meaning should causal or mechanistic inference be considered; at present none is warranted.",
  "research_notes": "Final report. Main validated negative-direction tracks: H16 feature_037=1, H39 feature_010=0 vs 1, H86 feature_002=0 vs 1, H139 feature_027=1. Conditional feature_063 supported in clean background and feature_038 high contexts: R213, H324/R281, H331/R288, H332/R289, H333/R290, H334/R291. H330 unresolved lower 0.119; H335/H336 no feature_036 support. Negative: markers, feature_024 interactions, most low-prevalence binaries, feature_003 residual, numeric feature_053, categorical probes. Unresolved deferred closed: H291,H295,H304,H315,H326. No new validation; next: external pre-specified feature_063 x feature_038 validation and multiplicity-aware model."
